# Notifier owns data loading — widgets display only

Screens and their `ScreenNotifier` load data, own cubits, and expose
action methods. Reusable widgets and screen **content** sections render
passed-in state — they do not fetch, navigate for data, or call cubits
directly.

## Owns loading / side effects (screen + notifier)

- `ScreenNotifier` fields: cubits, loading flags, cached GPS, init guards
- `initState` / `didChangeDependencies` on the **screen** shell: one-shot
  init that delegates to the notifier (e.g. `notifier.initializePrayerTimes`)
- Notifier methods: GPS fetch, cubit `initialize` / `refresh`, map picker
  → save location, retry, permission + location-service prompts
- `BlocListener` / `BlocConsumer` on the **screen content** layer (private
  host widget), wired to `notifier.someCubit` — not inside feature widgets

## Display only (widgets)

- Receive **state** and **callbacks** as constructor parameters
- No `context.read<Cubit>()`, `context.read<InternetProvider>()` for loads,
  `Nav.to` for data flows, or `getIt<UseCase>()` in widgets
- OK: `Theme.of`, `S.current`, formatting already-loaded entities, pure UI
  timers that only refresh displayed countdown text (clock passed from parent)

## Example

```dart
// ❌ BAD — feature widget fetches and drives cubit
class PrayerTimesSection extends StatefulWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final sn = context.read<HomeScreenNotifier>();
    return BlocConsumer<PrayerTimesCubit, PrayerTimesState>(
      bloc: sn.prayerTimesCubit,
      builder: (_, state) => ...,
    );
  }
  Future<void> _openMap() async {
    final result = await Nav.to(...);
    context.read<PrayerTimesCubit>().saveMapLocation(...);
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD — notifier + screen host; widget is dumb
class HomeScreenNotifier extends ScreenNotifier<HomeScreenParam> {
  final PrayerTimesCubit prayerTimesCubit = PrayerTimesCubit();

  Future<void> initializePrayerTimes({required bool hasInternet}) async { ... }
  Future<void> pickMapLocation(BuildContext context, {required bool hasInternet}) async { ... }
}

// home_screen_content.dart — private host wires bloc → display widget
BlocConsumer<PrayerTimesCubit, PrayerTimesState>(
  bloc: sn.prayerTimesCubit,
  builder: (_, state) => PrayerTimesSection(
    state: state,
    clock: _clock,
    onPickMapLocation: () => sn.pickMapLocation(context, hasInternet: hasInternet),
    onRetryGps: () => sn.retryPrayerGps(hasInternet: hasInternet),
  ),
);

class PrayerTimesSection extends StatelessWidget {
  const PrayerTimesSection({
    required this.state,
    required this.clock,
    required this.onPickMapLocation,
    required this.onRetryGps,
  });
  // build from state + callbacks only
}
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Cubits instantiated on `ScreenNotifier`, closed in `closeNotifier()`
- [ ] Screen shell triggers notifier init once (not in display widgets)
- [ ] `BlocConsumer` / listeners live in screen content, not shared widgets
- [ ] Feature widgets take state + `VoidCallback`s — no data I/O
- [ ] Navigation that returns data and triggers saves lives on the notifier
